completed_at: "2026-09-18T03:55:51.041Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: meet/event/remind live in builtin-calendar (package-owned commands) with full flag parity incl. scheduling presets and relative-time parsing; core alias shims keep old spellings working; uninstalling the package surfaces the owning-package hint (pm-b3e9 pattern); calendar shortcut specs pass via aliases
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Calendar package owns meet/event/remind commands and metadata through public SDK scheduling primitives; core registration is removed, legacy aliases and installation recovery remain, and nested discovery/help gates cover the package surface."
expected_result: Installed calendar commands and legacy aliases preserve scheduling semantics while core remains a reusable SDK baseline.
actual_result: "Real SDK and installed CLI acceptance passed for all shortcuts, flags, persistence, availability and uninstall recovery; full coverage is 100/100/100/100."
