  "2026-09-18T03:30:25.413Z","harness:codex","Migration gate fixes now pass focused tests (49 tests): full nested guide routing, retained calendar help budgets, and real installed package contracts. Pure command metadata is separated from SDK execution bindings so native Node gate imports do not need a workspace package self-link. In-process package SDK dispatch also verifies all three default scheduling handlers against persisted items."
  "2026-09-18T03:42:17.526Z","harness:codex","Final integration checks: package artifact smoke passed again after the metadata/runtime split; live telemetry flush drained the queue to zero. Static quality, docstrings, duplication, package/SDK parity, grammar, help budgets, refusal closure, agent-token gates, tracker-context quality, gate registry, and SDK snapshot checks passed. Import-cost checks initially exceeded budgets under simultaneous coverage load, then SDK and transport benchmarks passed after that load ended without changing limits. Validation retains the documented 170 unrecoverable historical resolution gaps; individual active histories match their latest records."
  "2026-09-18T03:55:48.309Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: 705 test files and 8,984 tests passed; statement coverage 64,769/64,769, branch coverage 49,414/49,414, function coverage 13,443/13,443 and line coverage 61,995/61,995, all 100%. No coverage exclusions or thresholds were added or relaxed. Linked pm tests passed. TypeScript, ESLint, zero-clone duplication scans, 100% source/export/member docstring gates, contracts, SDK parity, generated surfaces, guide routing and existing help budgets passed. All static stages passed; unchanged SDK import-cost and CLI transport budgets were rerun successfully without concurrent coverage load. Temporary Node and Bun manual sessions verified install/uninstall recovery, canonical and legacy scheduling, atomic refusal and calendar-month clamping. Packed npm/npx/bunx acceptance passed. Secret scan and dependency audit passed. Current GitHub security-alert inventories were empty. Sentry required gate passed with no unresolved issues; telemetry delivery drained the queue. Hosted PR checks and external reviews follow this local evidence and are independent claims."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T03:03:54.634Z","harness:codex","Architecture: calendar extension declares commands and flags over public SDK functions; generic SDK/MCP operation identities stay native. Core bootstrap retains legacy alias rewriting and missing-package recovery. Contract discovery distinguishes callable SDK actions from installed CLI commands."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T03:03:55.471Z","harness:codex","Host-owned global flags such as --author must not be registered by packages: extension activation rejects collisions. Real installed-package tests verify global identity forwarding and persisted history rather than mocking the registration layer."
  "2026-09-18T03:27:27.047Z","harness:codex",Package relocation must preserve the independent help budget inventory and full command-path documentation routing; a gate that matches only the root verb can silently lose or falsely reject nested capabilities. Keep negative controls for omitted package registration and parent/sibling confusion.
